2026-09-21 | Stage 2 signed-media-URL helpers | The media endpoints need a credential a browser can actually present, without relaxing the rule that the API TOKEN never travels in a URL | Added sign_media / media_url / media_signature_is_valid / media_expiry to web/api/auth.py, in the stdlib-only region so they stay importable in the pytest-only CI env. Three choices worth naming: the signature covers the DECODED (job_id, filename, exp) triple rather than request.url.path, because a minted URL must percent-encode the filename and the path does not -- signing the path would 401 on exactly the names containing a space or non-ASCII char and on no others; the payload is length-prefixed so ("a|b","c") and ("a","b|c") cannot collide; and the key is HMAC(token, context) rather than the token itself, so a captured signature gives nothing to grind against the real credential. exp is QUANTISED into buckets of ttl/2 -- without that, every response mints a different URL for the same file, and changing a <video> src tears down playback and discards the cached bytes | web/api/auth.py, tests/test_media_urls.py (37 tests)
2026-09-21 | Stage 3 require_token accepts a media signature -- the riskiest change in this task | This is the only edit that touches the authentication decision for every route in the application, and a mistake here FAILS OPEN SILENTLY: the authenticated path keeps working, so no ordinary test would notice | Scoped by what the signature ATTESTS, not by route, because tests/test_auth_token.py's AST guard requires every router to keep its dependencies= kwarg. Three conditions must all hold: path under /api/outputs/, BOTH job_id and filename present in request.path_params, and the HMAC over that exact triple verifying with exp in the future. Consequence worth noting: GET /api/outputs/{job_id} -- the directory listing -- has no filename param, so no signature can open it and the existing 401 assertion needed no change at all. VERIFIED NON-VACUOUS by mutation: breaking the prefix check, the expiry check, the compare_digest, or the fail-closed except each turns 1-7 tests red. The fifth mutation (dropping the filename half of condition 2) changes nothing, because media_signature_is_valid rejects an empty filename anyway -- that redundancy is now documented in the docstring rather than left looking tested | web/api/auth.py, tests/test_auth_token.py (+13 HTTP tests), tests/test_media_urls.py (+4 condition tests)
